# NORTHSTAR TEAM CHARTER

## 1. Project Name

Northstar Support Deflection MVP

## 2. Team Members

1. Nicole Muthee
2. Deirdre Sifuna
3. Pearl Nkosi
4. Wanyangu Flavius
5. Jesse Ochieng

## 3. Project Goal

The goal of Northstar is to create a self-service customer support
prototype that helps customers find answers without immediately
opening a support ticket.

The MVP covers:

- Order Status
- Returns & Refunds
- Stock Availability

## 4. Communication Rules

Team members will communicate regularly about project progress.

If a member is blocked, they should tell the team as soon as possible.

Team members should respond to important project messages promptly.

## 5. Deadlines

Each member is responsible for completing their assigned tasks
within the agreed project schedule.

If a member expects to miss a deadline, they must inform the team
before the deadline.

## 6. GitHub Rules

Each member will work on their assigned branch.

Members will make meaningful commits.

Commit messages will describe what changed and why.

Completed work should be submitted through a Pull Request for review.

## 7. Task Ownership

Each task has one main owner.

The owner is responsible for completing the Definition of Done.

The owner must keep the GitHub Project Board updated.

## 8. Board Status

TODO means the task has not started.

IN PROGRESS means the owner is actively working.

REVIEW means the owner has completed the work and another member
needs to check it.

DONE means the Definition of Done has been satisfied.

## 9. Conflict Resolution

If team members disagree:

1. Discuss the problem respectfully.
2. Check the project requirements.
3. Compare the possible solutions.
4. Agree on the best solution.
5. If necessary, Jesse coordinates the technical decision.
6. If the issue affects project requirements, Nicole coordinates
   the final project decision.

## 10. Contribution Expectations

Every member must make a meaningful contribution.

Members should complete their assigned tasks.

Members should help teammates when reasonable.

All contributions should be visible through GitHub history.

## 11. Escalation

If a member becomes unavailable or cannot complete their task,
the team should discuss the problem early and redistribute work
if necessary.

